hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1052","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam. My father and Shuaib informed us, saying: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Suwayd bin Qais told him, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed one day, then he gave his salaam and left, while he had remained in prayer one day.” rak'ah"
"1053","Bundar told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, my father told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Ayyub narrating, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suwayd. Ibn Qays, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Hudayj, said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at that time, so he gave the salutation in two rak’ahs, then he left, and he said to him: A man: “O Messenger of God, you made a mistake and said the salutation in two rak’ahs.” So he ordered Bilal and he established the prayer, then he completed that rak’ah. The people asked about the man. He said: O Messenger of God, you made a mistake. It was said to me: Do you know him? I said: No, unless I see him, then a man passed by me and I said: This is him. They said: This is Talha bin Ubaid Allah. This is the hadith of Bundar. Abu Bakr said: This story is not the story of Dhul-Yadin. Because the teacher of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made an oversight in this story, Talha bin Ubaid Allah, and the informant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in That is the story of Dhu al-Yadain, and the oversight on the part of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the story of Dhul-Yadayn only happened at noon or afternoon, and in this The story is that the forgetfulness occurred in Morocco, not at noon or in the afternoon. The story of Imran bin Husayn, the story of Al-Kharbaq, is a third story. Because the greeting in the story of Imran is from the third rak’ah, and in the story of Dhul-Yadayn from the two rak’ahs, and in the report of Imran the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered. his room, then he left the room, and according to the report of Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to a piece of wood displayed in the mosque, and everyone This is evidence that these stories are three stories: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a mistake once and said the two rak’ahs of prayer, and he made a mistake another time and said the salutation. In three rak'ahs, he eased it a third time and said the salaam in the two rak'ahs of sunset, so he spoke the three times, then he completed his prayer."
